  "tagline": "Streaming data lake for log-scale event data, with ClickHouse-based SQL over object storage.",
  "description": "Hydrolix is a commercial streaming data lake for very high-volume log and event data such as CDN, security and video telemetry. Streams are transformed on ingest, compressed into its own columnar, heavily indexed format on object storage, and queried through a ClickHouse-based SQL engine over the ClickHouse HTTP and native protocols, so Grafana, Kibana-style tools and Splunk connectors work on top. Compute is stateless on Kubernetes and scales separately from storage. It is usually deployed in the customer's cloud account and managed by Hydrolix, and Akamai resells it as TrafficPeak. The value is cheap long retention of full-fidelity data; the cost is a proprietary platform with usage-based contracts.",
